# Experiment configs are hashed byte-for-byte by checkpoint provenance.
# Pin checkout EOL so their SHA-256 values do not depend on core.autocrlf.
#
# Both files below are canonically LF. Their SHA-256 values are recorded
# inside the trained checkpoints and the run summaries, and the evaluation
# gate in src/ct_restoration/evaluation_integrity.py re-hashes the working
# file and refuses to score a checkpoint whose recorded hash no longer
# matches. Without these rules a CRLF checkout would fail provenance on a
# scientifically identical config.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only raw-byte-hashed experiment configs are pinned.
# The run summaries and training histories are read as JSON/CSV, never
# re-hashed, so their line endings cannot affect any gate. The checkpoints
# are hashed but are not tracked by Git.
configs/cnn.yaml   text eol=lf
configs/unet.yaml  text eol=lf
